---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Investor Overview — InTellMe"
  description="InTellMe builds evidence-governed research, verification, and decision infrastructure. Thesis, product status, milestones, and how research funding is kept separate from company investment."
  path="/investors"
>

  <!-- ── HERO: half viewport, more paper, less atmosphere ────── -->
  <section class="room" style="padding-top:96px;padding-bottom:64px" aria-labelledby="inv-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Investor overview</p>
      <h1 class="suite-title" id="inv-title" style="max-width:22ch">Evidence-governed infrastructure, and the products it makes possible.</h1>
      <hr class="rule--champagne" style="margin-top:32px" />
      <p class="hero-support" style="margin-top:28px">InTellMe develops evidence-governed AI infrastructure and turns that core capability into commercial products. TruVector and ResearchOne establish technical value. SAVR and one revenue product prove the company can ship and charge.</p>
      <div class="actions" style="margin-top:36px">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#request">Request Investor Materials</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#thesis">Read the thesis</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- ── THESIS + PROBLEM ───────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room" id="thesis" aria-labelledby="thesis-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Thesis</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="thesis-title">Consequential AI actions are taken on untraceable assertions.</h2>
      <div class="flagship reveal" style="margin-top:48px">
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p class="lede">As AI systems move from producing text to executing work, the operational question stops being whether a model said something wrong and becomes whether a system acted on something unreliable.</p>
          <p>Most of the surrounding tooling improves generation. Very little of it sits between the assertion and the action, and almost none of it leaves a record a reviewer can follow afterwards.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p>InTellMe builds the layer that evaluates an assertion before a downstream system acts on it, and keeps the evidence, the disagreement, and the reasoning attached to the result.</p>
          <p>That capability is the company. The commercial products are how it reaches a market and how the company funds itself while the core work is validated.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── PRODUCT SUMMARIES, SAME BADGES ─────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room room--alt" id="ships" aria-labelledby="ships-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">What the company ships</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="ships-title">Core technology, then commercial ventures.</h2>

      <ul class="rail reveal" style="margin-top:48px">
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">TruVector</span>
            <span class="badge">Validation and pilot development</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">Pre-execution arbitration of AI assertions before downstream systems act. States: Allow &middot; Review &middot; Block. One capability implemented, two under validation, one planned, two stated as hypotheses &mdash; the breakdown is published on the <a href="/#technology">Technology</a> section rather than summarised away.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">ResearchOne</span>
            <span class="badge">Private beta &mdash; early access available</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">Structured deep research that keeps sources, contradictions, reasoning lineage, and report contracts intact.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">SAVR</span>
            <span class="badge">Launching &mdash; web beta and Android testing</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">AI-assisted kitchen inventory and recipe planning that turns what you already have into meals.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">Golden Goose Tools</span>
            <span class="badge badge--live">Live</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">Instant technical SEO audit of a live page. Free audit; the complete list with fixes is $29 once.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">Golden Goose Studio</span>
            <span class="badge">Storefront in beta</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">AI-assisted product design with Printful-integrated placement, mockup, checkout, and fulfillment. Its first storefront, Golden Goose Tees, is open at goldengoosetees.com on live payments; unmarketed, and it has not yet taken a first order.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="product__meta" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="rail__name">wAether</span>
            <span class="badge badge--live">Live research product</span>
          </div>
          <span class="rail__note">A public observatory of solar, galactic, and terrestrial telemetry on official government data sources. Pricing starts at $4.99/month or $49.99/year.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── MILESTONES ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room" id="milestones" aria-labelledby="milestones-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Milestones</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="milestones-title">Where the work stands.</h2>
      <p class="caption reveal" style="margin-top:20px">Sequence, not calendar. Dates are published when they are committed.</p>
      <ul class="rail reveal">
        <li><span class="rail__name">TruVector</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">validation and pilot development.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">NSF SBIR Project Pitch</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">in preparation. Pursued, not awarded.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">ResearchOne</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">private beta, early access available.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">SAVR</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">web beta and Android testing.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">Golden Goose Studio</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">storefront in beta; unmarketed, first order still ahead.</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__name">wAether</span> &mdash; <span class="rail__note">live.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── COMMERCIALIZATION + FUNDING ────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room room--alt" id="funding" aria-labelledby="fund-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Commercialization model</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="fund-title">Research funding stays unmixed with company investment.</h2>

      <div class="tracks">
        <div class="track reveal">
          <h3 class="room-title">Track A &mdash; TruVector research funding</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:18px">An NSF SBIR Project Pitch is in preparation. It is being pursued, not awarded. The commercial applications are not the SBIR work, and are not represented as such.</p>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:24px">
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#request">Request TruVector Technical Brief</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="track reveal">
          <h3 class="room-title">Track B &mdash; Company investment</h3>
          <p style="margin-top:18px">Pre-seed and strategic capital. Use of funds, by category:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>TruVector validation and pilot operations</li>
            <li>ResearchOne private-beta hardening</li>
            <li>SAVR launch: evidence, evaluation, and documentation</li>
            <li>Company operations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:56px;padding-top:32px;border-top:1px solid var(--bronze-edge)">
        <h3 class="room-title">Funding status</h3>
        <p style="margin-top:16px">Development to date has been self-funded by the founder. <strong>InTellMe is pre-revenue across every application.</strong> Two products can take payment today; neither has produced revenue, and nothing here is presented as traction. What exists is shipped software and a technical thesis, not a customer base.</p>
        <p>InTellMe is the trade name under which Michael Brandon Lane, a sole proprietor in Johnson City, Tennessee, develops and operates these products. There is no outside capital, no debt, and no cap table. A Tennessee entity would be formed in connection with a first close.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── FOUNDER ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room" id="founder" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Founder</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="founder-title">One operator, in the open.</h2>
      <div class="flagship reveal" style="margin-top:40px">
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p class="lede">InTellMe is built and run by Michael Brandon Lane, from Johnson City, Tennessee.</p>
          <p>His training is in chemical engineering, where a number is worth nothing until you can say how it was measured and within what error. That is the whole thesis behind TruVector: a system about to act on an assertion should be able to show its work first.</p>
          <p>He is the only engineer on everything here. TruVector, ResearchOne, SAVR, Golden Goose Studio, and wAether were designed, built, and shipped by one person, self-funded, in public.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flagship__pane">
          <p>What that buys: a very short line between a decision and a deployed change, and a founder who has already shown he finishes things without a budget.</p>
          <p>What it costs: bandwidth, and a commercial function that does not exist yet. Both are named in the use of funds rather than papered over.</p>
          <ul class="facts">
            <li>Public code &mdash; <a href="https://github.com/GooseyPrime" rel="noopener">github.com/GooseyPrime</a></li>
            <li>Direct &mdash; <a href="mailto:brandon@intellmeai.com">brandon@intellmeai.com</a></li>
            <li>Johnson City, Tennessee</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── REQUEST FORM ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room room--alt" id="request" aria-labelledby="request-title">
    <div class="suite">
      <p class="kicker">Request</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="request-title">Request investor materials.</h2>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top:20px;max-width:56ch">The deck, technical briefs, roadmap, use of funds, IP summary, and demo access are sent after review. Nothing is attached automatically.</p>

      <form class="form reveal" id="investor-form" method="post" action="/api/investor-request">
        <input type="hidden" name="_started" id="_started" value="" />
        <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
          <label for="company_website">Company website</label>
          <input type="text" id="company_website" name="company_website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>

        <div class="field">
          <label for="name">Name <span class="req">(required)</span></label>
          <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required autocomplete="name" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="email">Email <span class="req">(required)</span></label>
          <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="organization">Organization</label>
          <input type="text" id="organization" name="organization" autocomplete="organization" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="role">Role</label>
          <input type="text" id="role" name="role" autocomplete="organization-title" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="want">What you are looking for</label>
          <select id="want" name="want">
            <option value="Technical brief">Technical brief</option>
            <option value="Investor materials" selected>Investor materials</option>
            <option value="Demo access">Demo access</option>
            <option value="Other">Other</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="found">How you found InTellMe</label>
          <input type="text" id="found" name="found" />
        </div>
        <div class="field field--wide">
          <label for="message">Message</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="5"></textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="field field--wide actions" style="margin-top:8px">
          <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Send request</button>
          <span class="caption">Or write directly to <a href="mailto:brandon@intellmeai.com?subject=Investor%20materials">brandon@intellmeai.com</a>.</span>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .form { display: grid; gap: 24px 32px; margin-top: 40px; max-width: 720px; }
  @media (min-width: 768px) { .form { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .field { display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .field--wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .form label {
    font-family: var(--label); font-weight: 500; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--stone-text);
  }
  .req { letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: none; color: var(--stone-text); }
  .form input, .form select, .form textarea {
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--smoked-bronze);
    color: var(--ivory);
    border: 1px solid var(--bronze-edge);
    border-radius: 1px;
    padding: 13px 14px;
    font-family: var(--body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.4;
    min-height: 44px;
    transition: border-color var(--t-micro) var(--ease-lobby);
  }
  .form textarea { min-height: 120px; resize: vertical; }
  .form input:hover, .form select:hover, .form textarea:hover { border-color: var(--bronze-edge-hot); }
  /* Invalid state is carried by weight and an inset edge as well as by hue,
     so it is perceivable without distinguishing red from bronze. */
  .form input:user-invalid, .form textarea:user-invalid {
    border-color: var(--danger);
    box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--danger);
  }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
</style>
